  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Sunday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: An upper-level area of low pressure will\nprogress southward across California this afternoon. This cyclone\naloft will pivot eastward and progress through Southern Nevada\ntonight. Rain chances will be highest in Southeastern White Pine\nCounty today and tonight. A few strong thunderstorms are\nconceivable in Eastern Nevada this afternoon into this evening.\nThe primary thunderstorm hazards will be wind gusts near 50 mph \nand dangerous cloud to ground lightning strikes.\n\nA ridge of high pressure will build across Northern Nevada Tuesday\nthrough Thursday. An anticyclone aloft will be centered over\nSouthern California Friday. This upper-level area of high pressure\nwill move eastward across the Desert Southwest this weekend. A\nwarming trend is expected Tuesday through Thursday. By Thursday\nafternoon, high temperatures in Northern and Central Nevada will\nbe around ten degrees above normal. Temperatures will remain well\nabove seasonal values Friday through Sunday. Here are\nprobabilities of maximum temperatures of 80 degrees or higher for\nselect locations in Northern and Central Nevada on Friday, October\n2nd, 2026: \n\nTonopah - 97%\nElko - 95%\nBattle Mountain - 95%\nCarlin - 95%\nEureka - 95%\nWinnemucca - 90%\nEly - 90%\nWells - 90%\nSpring Creek - 85%\nWest Wendover - 80%\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High forecast confidence\nregarding the possibility of a few strong thunderstorms in Eastern\nNevada this afternoon into this evening. High forecast confidence\nin the likelihood of showers in East Central Nevada today. High\nforecast confidence regarding a warming trend Tuesday through\nThursday. Moderate forecast confidence in temperatures remaining\nwell above seasonal values Friday through Sunday. No deviations\nfrom the NBM model output.",
